  "slug": "quantum-circuit-compilation-0208",
  "summary": "New preprints tie compilation to hardware cost: pulse latency in SCOPE and two-qubit counts in quspect, alongside faster noisy and QEC circuit simulation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is compilation judged by hardware-level cost rather than abstract gate count. SCOPE uses an operator Schmidt time surrogate to reduce pulse execution latency and is reported to outperform EPOC on 104 benchmarks. The quspect SDK selects routings after coupling-constrained resynthesis, reaching 0.616x the two-qubit gates of Qiskit O3 on 55 circuits across five targets. A second, adjacent thread concerns classical simulation of noisy and error-corrected circuits: MASQ, pre-trajectory sampling with mid-circuit measurements and general Kraus channels, and Clifford-augmented matrix product states for coherent noise. The QAOA coverage study uses exact references and hardware diagnostics, and the fluid-flow paper pairs reduced models with surface-code estimates; both are application-side rather than compilation results.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
